From 8f27e705143fb26dd9bf43a4784000f59c5a740d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Mon, 16 Nov 2026 20:45:30 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Support several keys and claim checks in JWT authentication

- New 'keys' option: a list of keys with an optional 'kid', tried in order,
  so signing keys can be rotated without downtime. 'secret' and 'algorithm'
  are now optional when 'keys' are given.
- New optional 'issuer', 'audience' and 'domain_key' claim checks.
- Malformed tokens and unset environment variables are rejected instead of
  crashing the authentication process.
- The token claims are no longer logged on successful authentication.
- stop/1 now erases the stored key.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01ETaRHXo1LmPHqZB9SXMucM
